# ---- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# The OC Transpo subscription key. .env.example is committed. .env never is.
#
# The program looks in three places, in this order: the environment, ./.env,
# and ~/.config/otransit/.env. The third is the one to use, because both
# implementations of this program read it, and one key on disk is better than
# two.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Go build output -----------------------------------------------------
# The binary, anchored to the repository root. Without the leading slash this
# would also ignore a package directory of the same name, such as
# cmd/otransit/.
/otransit
/otransit-go
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Compiled test binaries, from `go test -c`.
*.test

# Modules come from the proxy. Nothing is vendored.
/vendor/

# Workspace files are per-machine.
go.work
go.work.sum

# ---- test and profiling output -------------------------------------------
# Careful: *.out is the Go convention for a coverage profile, and it is wide.
# A file named go.out or rust.out disappears without a word. Write the
# conformance comparison outside this repository.
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
*.prof
*.pprof

# Fuzzing corpora found by `go test -fuzz`. Check one in by hand when it
# reproduces a real defect. Leave the rest here.
testdata/fuzz/

# ---- feed data and caches ------------------------------------------------
# The GTFS download and anything unpacked from it. Fetched by the update
# command, never committed.
*.zip
/gtfs/
/gtfs-extract/
/data/
/samples/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---- editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- the conformance directory -------------------------------------------
# A symlink to the reference checkout, so `make diff` needs no absolute path.
# The link is per-machine, so it stays out of the repository.
#
# Remove this rule on the day conformance/ becomes a real submodule at the same
# path. Git ignores a submodule that an ignore rule covers, and it says nothing
# while it does.
/conformance

# ---- assistant and local config ------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# Skills cloned from their own repositories. Each one carries a nested .git,
# which git would record as an embedded repository. They update with
# `git pull`. To vendor one instead, drop this rule and delete its .git first.
/.claude/skills/

# ---- documentation is tracked, with one exception ------------------------
# There is deliberately no *.md rule here. Ignore a document by name when it is
# genuinely local, and never ignore the category.
#
# The other implementation ignored *.md and named the exceptions. CLAUDE.md was
# never added to that list, so the file holding every trap in the codebase sat
# untracked for the life of the project and reached no clone.
#
# CLAUDE.md is local here by choice, and this is the lesson from that: what it
# held about the program did not go with it. The traps are in TRAPS.md, the four
# rules that keep a replay honest are in PORTING.md, and the mutation campaign's
# vocabulary is in TESTING.md. Nothing a clone needs lives only in the file
# below.
/CLAUDE.md
